# Local build output.
#
# GitHub Pages publishes this site from the `gh-pages` branch via a
# workflow (checked: source.branch=gh-pages, build_type=workflow), so
# `docs/` here is only ever a local build artefact — caches, generated
# JSON reports, copied assets. Committing it would put ~20 regenerated
# files into every diff for no gain.
#
# `docs/i18n-followup.md` is the exception: it is hand-written, predates
# the build output, and is tracked. It is kept at its historical path
# rather than moved, so its history stays intact.
/docs/*
!/docs/i18n-followup.md
